  "audits": [
    {
      "source_id": "DCP-LETT-1646",
      "target_id": "DCP-LETT-1815",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": "1646 is the surviving Fox incoming response to Darwin’s earlier Cock-and-Hen request: it reports searches for the old Dorking and Cochin cocks and Captain Hornby, while preserving fear that Darwin has received none. The later 1843 source is not needed to establish this reverse reply.",
      "response_scope": "1646 surviving body paragraphs 1–4 in response to 1815’s poultry request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1815",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "Thanks for your letter: I had your name on my list to write to soon to tell you how I got on in the Cock & Hen line of business. I have got nothing but promises as yet, & there are few or none like you, who do what they ",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-1815.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "2d0429f5f68386370a1d4d97fab86adf1ad095bc07caa0e6cae610262ee7f62a",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "77b5b6213ac1b1e343478712be9e8abf4e30a8b4f9e3900ba6ef88edd3b93c2d"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1646",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I have anxiously inspected My Dorking & Cochin friends Yards for an old Cock of Each, & written to Captain Hornby —but I fear you have not received any yet. There must be some die before long I think.",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-1646.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "a8a54e08a3f62bbbc5b6db52f4e2153707b6c4c47549ed3d4305b4053527142b",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "8bb4317f83dd79691af7f930200dd280e7a99fe91af043335db74d6df30fd71f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_id": "DCP-LETT-1843",
      "target_id": "DCP-LETT-1646",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": "1843 is Darwin’s partial reply to Fox’s incoming poultry and hound report: it acknowledges the Scotch Deer Hound triumph and asks to hear further kennel information. Scope excludes unrelated geological and domestic sections.",
      "response_scope": "1843 body paragraphs 1–2; antecedent poultry/hound material in 1646.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1646",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I have anxiously inspected My Dorking & Cochin friends Yards for an old Cock of Each, & written to Captain Hornby —but I fear you have not received any yet. There must be some die before long I think.",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-1646.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "a8a54e08a3f62bbbc5b6db52f4e2153707b6c4c47549ed3d4305b4053527142b",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "8bb4317f83dd79691af7f930200dd280e7a99fe91af043335db74d6df30fd71f"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1843",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I was very glad to get your note & congratulate you on your triumph about the Scotch Deer Hound, which however I do not know by sight.— How I wish I further knew (can you find out for me) whether the real Scotch Deer Hou",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-1843.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "f48c60c535d1881e9b06c1879bb9e8f65c11343479d8093365646e8edbf051ab",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "fa5f9d34cb67ad16ebb9f6903bf6255d4ea421d97f32f78c06c8e5da4e550e61"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_id": "DCP-LETT-11799",
      "target_id": "DCP-LETT-1978",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": "11799’s later Fox health letter supplies the surviving follow-up to Darwin’s concern about Malvern, Dr Gully and the douche. It is a health update, not evidence that every earlier specimen or book request was answered.",
      "response_scope": "11799 health paragraphs only; 1978’s health concern, not its unrelated subjects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1978",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I am so sorry to hear of all your suffering: it is most grievous that you should so soon fall back after Malvern, & how patiently you seem to bear it. I suppose the pain is extremely severe: very oddly I had yesterday mo",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-1978.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "78f9e2e0cbbd1a47d469cf5c308a07bdfac46b233b0c5b1ac668eb994d3e1467",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "1e2a47de79773087f7d3ff1260a7551872f0ff9596ec51088db73d93b27cb1c3"
        },
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-11799",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I am got back from Malvern very much better for Dr Gully. I sadly miss the Douche here & wish I had yours. My substitutes are 3 pails of water thrown over me on rising before a shallow—& 6 minutes water poured down spine",
          "source_path": "data/raw/dcp/1856-1857/pages/DCP-LETT-11799.html",
          "source_html_sha256": "4cbde6b939e6b810d9f2376a0cefa1e086fb34cde09320d0f33e5f2f3d5b2fcb",
          "dom_locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1",
          "source_xml_sha256": "ded00810be15e5f8ea107761077ebfe7068fc1216d7e5330d3668526ec1092b1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
